# Coverage gate (90% minimum)

Before finishing work that will merge to **main**:

1. Run `npm run test:coverage` — must pass with **≥ 90%** on lines, statements, functions, and branches for scoped modules (backend: `csvAnalyze`, `categorize`, `openrouter`; frontend: utils listed in `vitest.config.js`).
2. Run `npm run build` — coverage runs **before** compile steps; do not reorder `scripts/build.mjs` to build first.
3. Do not lower `COVERAGE_THRESHOLD` in `scripts/coverage-threshold.mjs` or vitest thresholds to bypass CI.

CI on **main** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) blocks merge when coverage or build fails. Local **pre-push** hook runs `test:coverage`.

When adding code in scoped paths, add or extend tests in the same PR — do not commit untested logic to main-bound branches.
